{"nodes": [{"id": "design_v4_00_ai_schedule_architect_ai_schedule_architect", "label": "AI Schedule Architect", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "design/v4/00-ai-schedule-architect.md", "source_location": "\u00a72", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Replaces the retired prose\u2192constraints AI (scheduling.ai v1) which only translated prose into a constraints jsonb and was judged not good enough; its plumbing (entitlement key, kill-switch, env, SDK dep, error conventions) is kept so this ships as a replacement, not a new SKU."}, {"id": "design_v4_00_ai_schedule_architect_three_modes", "label": "Three modes, one pipeline (generate / refine / repair)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "design/v4/00-ai-schedule-architect.md", "source_location": "\u00a72", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "generate seeds from a greedy draft, refine re-uses the prior proposal, repair scopes the movable set and turns everything outside scope into obstacles \u2014 one pipeline avoids three code paths."}, {"id": "design_v4_00_ai_schedule_architect_propose_only", "label": "Propose-only endpoint contract", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "design/v4/00-ai-schedule-architect.md", "source_location": "\u00a72", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Nothing persists until the organiser accepts, so the AI feature adds zero new write machinery \u2014 accept reuses applySchedule with its transaction, advisory lock, ledger event and seq bump."}, {"id": "design_v4_00_ai_schedule_architect_build_schedule_pack", "label": "buildSchedulePack (context pack builder)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "design/v4/00-ai-schedule-architect.md", "source_location": "\u00a73.1", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "design_v4_00_ai_schedule_architect_slot_fixtures_draft", "label": "slotFixtures greedy draft", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "design/v4/00-ai-schedule-architect.md", "source_location": "\u00a73.2", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A legal-but-naive baseline so the LLM improves on a schedule instead of inventing time math from scratch; the free/Pro Auto-schedule button is unchanged and AI is a layer above it."}, {"id": "design_v4_00_ai_schedule_architect_validate_assignments_referee", "label": "validateAssignments referee", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "design/v4/00-ai-schedule-architect.md", "source_location": "\u00a73.4", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Binding decision 'LLM plans, engine referees' \u2014 no proposal reaches the DB without passing validateAssignments and assertNoBlocking inside the apply transaction."}, {"id": "design_v4_00_ai_schedule_architect_repair_round_loop", "label": "Repair round loop (max 2)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "design/v4/00-ai-schedule-architect.md", "source_location": "\u00a73.4", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Blocking conflicts are fed back as a conflict report asking for minimal fixes; capped at 2 rounds, then the best proposal returns with residual conflicts marked blocking so the UI can disable accept."}, {"id": "design_v4_00_ai_schedule_architect_ai_plan_endpoint", "label": "POST /api/v1/divisions/{id}/schedule/ai-plan", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "design/v4/00-ai-schedule-architect.md", "source_location": "\u00a74", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "design_v4_00_ai_schedule_architect_competition_ai_plan_endpoint", "label": "POST /api/v1/competitions/{id}/schedule/ai-plan", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "design/v4/00-ai-schedule-architect.md", "source_location": "\u00a74", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "design_v4_00_ai_schedule_architect_stateless_conversation", "label": "Stateless conversation (no ai_sessions table)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "design/v4/00-ai-schedule-architect.md", "source_location": "\u00a78.2", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The client holds the conversation and posts the prior proposal back on refine; revisit only if transcripts must survive reloads."}, {"id": "design_v4_00_ai_schedule_architect_schedule_source_ai", "label": "fixtures.schedule_source = 'ai' migration", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "design/v4/00-ai-schedule-architect.md", "source_location": "\u00a75", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Only schema change in the wave \u2014 proposals are ephemeral client state and the applied result is fully captured by the existing ledger + checkpoint machinery, so no new tables."}, {"id": "design_v4_00_ai_schedule_architect_gating_order", "label": "Gate order: auth \u2192 kill-switch \u2192 entitlement \u2192 rate limit \u2192 validation", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "design/v4/00-ai-schedule-architect.md", "source_location": "\u00a76", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The PostHog ai-scheduling kill-switch is evaluated before the billing gate so a global off-switch never surfaces an upgrade prompt."}, {"id": "design_v4_00_ai_schedule_architect_failure_taxonomy", "label": "AI plan failure taxonomy (503/402/422/409/429)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "design/v4/00-ai-schedule-architect.md", "source_location": "\u00a77", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Flexible divisions have no timestamps to plan (409 AI_PLAN_UNSUPPORTED) and >500 movable fixtures both match the apply limit and bound the context pack (422 AI_PLAN_TOO_LARGE)."}, {"id": "design_v4_00_ai_schedule_architect_constraint_suggestions", "label": "Opt-in constraint_suggestions", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "design/v4/00-ai-schedule-architect.md", "source_location": "\u00a78.6", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Suggestions never auto-write settings; the UI shows a checked-by-default list applied on accept via the existing schedule-settings PUT, so there is no new write endpoint."}, {"id": "design_v4_00_ai_schedule_architect_before_ai_checkpoint", "label": "before-ai auto-checkpoint", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "design/v4/00-ai-schedule-architect.md", "source_location": "\u00a75", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Created in the accept flow before apply via existing schedule.versioning checkpoints so every AI apply has one-click undo."}], "edges": [{"source": "design_v4_00_ai_schedule_architect_ai_schedule_architect", "target": "design_v4_00_ai_schedule_architect_three_modes", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "design/v4/00-ai-schedule-architect.md", "source_location": "\u00a72", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "design_v4_00_ai_schedule_architect_three_modes", "target": "design_v4_00_ai_schedule_architect_propose_only", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "design/v4/00-ai-schedule-architect.md", "source_location": "\u00a72", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "design_v4_00_ai_schedule_architect_build_schedule_pack", "target": "design_v4_00_ai_schedule_architect_slot_fixtures_draft", "relation": "calls", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "design/v4/00-ai-schedule-architect.md", "source_location": "\u00a73", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "design_v4_00_ai_schedule_architect_repair_round_loop", "target": "design_v4_00_ai_sche